Innovation experience HUB (innexHUB), Digital Innovation Hub of East Lombardy, was established in July 2017 as a non-profit association by the Industrial Associations of Brescia, Cremona and Mantova and two craftmanship associations located in Brescia. The aim was to create a subject focused on spreading the digital culture among SMEs, making them aware of: what being digital means, what KETs are, how the digital is rapidly transforming business models and the current and future opportunities / threats linked to digital technologies.
innexHUB has two additional purposes: to help enterprises understand their digital maturity level and identify the subsequent actions to digitally evolve as well as to guide enterprises in their digital transformation paths, ensuring they can rely on trustworthy suppliers.
During 2017 and 2018 innexHUB strengthened its governance by engaging with 6 new shareholders (associations and confederations) representing 3 additional sectors: Agriculture, Construction and Commerce, Tourism and Hospitality Services. As of now innexHUB action field encompasses and addresses 4 sectors (Industry; Agriculture; Construction; Commerce, Tourism and Hospitality Services) as well as 1 horizontal cluster (Craftmanship) made of micro and small enterprises across different sectors.
It is worthy to mention that 2 Universities figure among innexHUB shareholders and their technical and scientific contribution is essential for the hubs&rsquo; governance and orientation (e.g., representatives from both Universities have a seat in the hub&rsquo;s Technical and Scientific Committee).
Altogether innexHUB partners (shareholders) represent more than 50.000 SMEs located in the provinces of Brescia, Cremona and Mantova, equalling a third of the total population of active enterprises in the three provinces listed above.
In 2018 innexHUB has become fully operational by developing a catalogue of services that includes:
&bull; Awareness creation: design and organization of seminars and workshops centred around the increasing role and opportunities of KETs and digitalization as well as the provision and dissemination of information / materials (e.g. videos and reports on best practices / success cases) by means of the hub&rsquo;s website, e-learning platform and social channels;
&bull; Digital Maturity assessment: development and administration of digital maturity / readiness assessments, both in self-assisted (freely accessible web-based application) and assisted modes (on premises interviews), to evaluate an enterprise current state of digital readiness (i.e., processes, products, tools, skills) and identify possible evolutionary trajectories;
&bull; Ecosystem building, scouting, brokerage, networking: development of a catalogue of certified suppliers providing technical consulting in the design and implementation of digitalization projects as well as continuous training and education opportunities around digital topics to boost workforce upskilling;
&bull; Access to funding: dissemination of digital innovation funding opportunities and support to SMEs in accessing to public and private funding instruments;
&bull; Mentoring: support prior and during the implementation of digital transformation projects;
&bull; Education and skills development: co-creation, in partnership with external organizations, of training and education courses providing intelligence on SMEs&rsquo; needs and how to better address them.

Confindustria Brescia was founded on the 14th of April 1897. It is the oldest Italian entrepreneurial organization, having been active for over 110 years. As part of the Confindustria system, the Association represents the industrial and services sectors in the province of Brescia in all the political, institutional, administrative and trade union bodies, both local and national, in order to safeguard their interests.
This Representation is coordinated with other trade associations operating in the province of Brescia to protect the general interests of industry and the competitiveness of the economy of Brescia.
Confindustria Brescia now brings together more than 1,300 large, small and medium-sized enterprises operating in different sectors and employing a labour force of over 67,000 people.

Mission and objectives
The main mission of the Confindustria Brescia is to support entrepreneurial culture, to promote the development of the area. Members of the Confindustria Brescia can be industrial firms and consortiums producing goods and offering services.
The main objectives of the Confindustria Brescia are:
&middot; to encourage the spreading of entrepreneurial culture to develop the local economy through the promotion of innovation, the high quality of products and the improvement of production processes.
&middot; to pursue sustainable growth of industrial activities by providing assistance, consulting, and training courses to companies.
&middot; to develop competitiveness and the international aspect of industry in the area of Brescia.
&middot; to promote a closer link between education and the production system.
&middot; to assist the growth of employment and enhance the qualification of the workforce through training courses.
&middot; to contribute to improving the local infrastructure facilities. 
&middot; to strengthen interaction with local institutions and trade unions in order to develop the industrial framework of the province of Brescia along with the competitiveness of all firms.

Services
The Association, with all its various operational areas, offers services in crucial areas forentrepreneurial activities:
&middot; Relations with trade unions; 
&middot; Human resources management; 
&middot; Labour standards and norms; 
&middot; Safety and the environment; 
&middot; Communication and media relations; 
&middot; Training; 
&middot; Credit and finance; 
&middot; Internationalization;
&middot; Tax and company law;
&middot; Environmental issues; 
&middot; Information about the association&rsquo;s sectors and the protection of industrial and commercial property; 
&middot; Innovation; 
&middot; Energy and Climate
&middot; Soustenaibility
&middot; European affairs and legal monitoring
&middot; PA regulation e and relations
&middot; Legal

